      "writtenOn": "2026-01-07T21:13:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is eventually the focus of this change: allow more Gerrit contributors by removing the `Release-Notes: skip` requirement.\n\nI am happy to give it a go for the next release and measure:\n- How many more contributions we have thanks to this relaxation of the rule\n- How the quality is impacted (or not impacted) by not having this footer\n\n@milutin@google.com do you guys use Germini (or other AI) with MCP for extracting the release notes? Or do you simply build them as a summary of the commit message?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "2c8c67a9828ae39e174dbc99e20aa7dabc306bb5",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
